; viveka-max: the comparative that selects the greater value.
; "heavier", "faster", "bigger", "taller" etc. all express this:
; given two values of the same concept, find the one that is greater.
; 
; viveka = discernment. max = the greater side of the discernment.
; the proof graph holds both — viveka-max names the direction.
; 
; when this word appears in a question with two entities, the pipeline
; dispatches to viveka-ganana with direction="max".

(kosha viveka-max
  (vishesa logic-varga)
  (swarupa viveka)
  (abheda max)
  (yukta comparison inference))
